:: Bedroom [clearing] {"position":"1250,1725","size":"100,100"}
''THE BEDROOM''

You step into a quiet bedroom.

The colors are muted.

A bed sits beside a small table.

There are photographs, books, and unfinished paintings.

You notice that the objects in this room resemble things you discovered throughout the garden.

A journal lies open.

"Sometimes I feel like I am living in two different worlds.

But they both belong to me."

You begin to understand.

The garden was never just a garden.

It was someone's mind.

[[Examine the photograph->Photograph]]


:: Central Clearing [clearing] {"position":"1050,1600","size":"100,100"}
# THE CENTRAL CLEARING

The garden becomes strangely quiet.

You finally reach the center of the maze.

A circular stone platform stands before you.

The flowers around it resemble the ones
you discovered at the beginning.

(if: $visitedLeft and $visitedRight and $gateOpen and $symbolSolved)[

The symbols on the platform illuminate.

A portal begins to form.

(set: $portalOpen to true)

You hear a voice:

"You have walked through my thoughts.

But you have not yet met me."

[[Approach the portal->Portal]]

]
(else:)[

The platform remains dormant.

You feel that something is still missing.

[[Return to the maze->Overgrown Path]]

]


:: Changing Landscape [clearing] {"position":"1250,1475","size":"100,100"}
# THE CHANGING LANDSCAPE

The world begins to change around you.

(if: $ideas >= 4)[

The colors seem increasingly intense.

Objects move before you can focus on them.

You hear several overlapping voices.

There is so much happening
that you struggle to process it.

]

(else:)[

The world continues to shift.

The flowers move through the air.

The sky changes color.

You feel both fascinated and disoriented.

]

You begin to wonder whether
this place is really an escape.

A small building appears in the distance.

[[Approach the building->Gardener's Journal]]


:: Cracked Mirror [heaviness] {"position":"875,850","size":"100,100"}
# THE CRACKED MIRROR

A large mirror stands between two trees.

Your reflection looks unfamiliar.

You notice several cracks running across the glass.

You lean closer.

The reflection looks exhausted.

A message is engraved into the frame:

"Is this how you see yourself?"

(set: $awareness to $awareness + 1)

[[Continue down the pathway->Forgotten Letter]]


:: Ending [clearing] {"position":"1425,1475","size":"100,100"}
''THE GARDENER''

(if: $endingChoice is "understand")[
You look around the garden.

You have learned its pathways.

You have discovered its memories.

But exploring someone's mind does not mean you have experienced their life.

The garden is still unfamiliar.
]
(else-if: $endingChoice is "uncertain")
[
You look around the garden.

You recognize that there are things you cannot fully comprehend.

Perhaps acknowledging that is the beginning of understanding.
]
(else-if: $endingChoice is "listen")
[
You look around the garden.

You realize that observing someone's experiences is not the same as living them.

You may never fully understand what the Gardener experiences.

But you can listen.
]
(else:)[
You pause, unsure how to answer.

Perhaps the most honest beginning is to remain curious and listen.
]

The flowers begin to move in the breeze.

For the first time, the garden feels peaceful.

A final message appears:

"You came looking for a way out.

But perhaps the garden was never a place to escape.

Perhaps it was a place to learn how to look."

''THE END.''

Thank you for exploring the Gardener's world.

(link: "Begin a new journey")[(restart:)]


:: Endless Staircase [heaviness] {"position":"875,725","size":"100,100"}
# THE ENDLESS STAIRCASE

A staircase disappears into the fog.

You begin climbing.

One step.

Another step.

Another.

The top never seems to get closer.

You wonder whether reaching the top will actually change anything.

A message appears on the wall:

"Sometimes the hardest part is simply beginning."

[[Continue through the trees->Cracked Mirror]]


:: Final Question [clearing] {"position":"1250,2100","size":"100,100"}
''THE FINAL QUESTION''

You have explored the garden.

You have experienced its heaviness and its overwhelming brightness.

You have discovered its memories.

You have learned about the Gardener.

A final message appears:

"You have walked through my garden.

You've seen my flowers bloom and wither.

You've opened my doors and followed my paths.

So tell me.

What have you learned?"

(link: "I think I understand what it feels like.")[
(set: $endingChoice to "understand")
(go-to: "Ending")
]

(link: "I don't think I can fully understand.")[
(set: $endingChoice to "uncertain")
(go-to: "Ending")
]

(link: "I cannot fully understand, but I can listen.")[
(set: $endingChoice to "listen")
(go-to: "Ending")
]


:: Floating Garden [clearing] {"position":"1050,1975","size":"100,100"}
# THE FLOATING GARDEN

You discover a garden filled with floating objects.

Stars.

Books.

Paintings.

Unfinished projects.

Everything seems equally important.

You feel drawn toward every object.

(link: "Follow the floating books")[
    (set: $ideas to $ideas + 1)
    (go-to: "Changing Landscape")
]

(link: "Explore the glowing flowers")[
    (set: $ideas to $ideas + 1)
    (go-to: "Changing Landscape")
]


:: Floating Library [excess] {"position":"1000,1100","size":"100,100"}
# THE FLOATING LIBRARY

Books float around you.

Each contains a different story.

One book begins speaking.

Another opens by itself.

A third book falls directly into your hands.

You feel compelled to explore everything.

What will you do?

[[Read one book carefully->Library Memory]]

[[Try to explore everything at once->Unfinished Projects]]


:: Flower Result [heaviness] {"position":"600,1000","size":"100,100"}
# THE FLOWER BED

(if: $weight is 1)[
You manage to water the flowers.

One begins to bloom.
]

(if: $weight is 2)[
You struggle to continue.

The watering can feels heavier than before.

You sit down beside the flowers.
]

(if: $weight >= 3)[
You look at the flowers.

Even beginning another task feels exhausting.

You wonder why something so small
can feel so difficult.
]

A small pathway leads out of the greenhouse.

[[Follow the pathway->Overgrown Path]]


:: Forgotten Fountain [heaviness] {"position":"600,1250","size":"100,100"}
# THE FORGOTTEN FOUNTAIN

A dry fountain stands in the center of the pathway.

Three symbols are carved into its surface.

A key.

A flower.

A letter.

You recognize them from your journey.

(if: $keyFound)[
The key symbol begins to glow.
]

(if: $flowerFound)[
The flower symbol begins to glow.
]

(if: $letterFound)[
The letter symbol begins to glow.
]

You hear a faint mechanical sound.

Something is hidden nearby.

[[Investigate the garden shed->Garden Shed]]


:: Forgotten Letter [heaviness] {"position":"875,975","size":"100,100"}
# THE FORGOTTEN LETTER

You discover an unfinished letter beneath a flowerpot.

The handwriting is difficult to read.

"I don't know how to explain it.

Sometimes getting out of bed feels like climbing a mountain.

I know there are things I should do.

I just cannot seem to find the energy to begin."

(if: $letterFound is false)[
    (set: $letterFound to true)
    (set: $memory to $memory + 1)
]

You place the letter in your pocket.

[[Continue toward the greenhouse->Overgrown Greenhouse]]


:: Garden Entrance {"position":"875,350","size":"100,100"}
# THE MAZE ENTRANCE

You try to look beyond past the trees and hedges, and realize you are in a gigantic garden.

A rusted iron gate hangs open in front of you.

Beyond it, two pathways twist and turn away from each other.

One is dark, overgrown, and strangely quiet.

The other glows with an unusual golden light, almost breathing on its own.

A wooden sign reads:

"Every path leads somewhere.
Not every path leads you home."

[[Approach the signpost->Signpost]]


:: Garden Shed [heaviness] {"position":"600,1375","size":"100,100"}
# THE GARDEN SHED

An old wooden shed stands behind the fountain.

Inside, you discover gardening tools,
old photographs, and scattered notes.

A small inscription is written on the wall:

"Three things are needed to remember."

You recognize the symbols from the fountain.

A narrow path leads toward a large gate.

[[Continue toward the gate->Locked Gate]]


:: Gardener's Journal [clearing] {"position":"1250,1600","size":"100,100"}
''THE GARDENER'S JOURNAL''

An old journal rests on a wooden table.

You open it.

The handwriting is familiar.

You begin reading.

"Sometimes I feel like my thoughts are moving faster than I can write them."

"Sometimes getting out of bed feels impossible."

"Sometimes I have so many plans that I cannot decide where to begin."

You recognize the two gardens.

The heaviness.

The brightness.

They both belong to the same person.

(if: $journalFound is false)[
(set: $journalFound to true)
(set: $memory to $memory + 1)
(set: $awareness to $awareness + 1)
]

A final entry catches your attention:

"I wish people understood that I am still myself, even when my experiences change."

[[Explore the nearby bedroom->Bedroom]]


:: Gardener's Voice [clearing] {"position":"1250,1975","size":"100,100"}
''THE GARDENER'S VOICE''

The room becomes quiet.

You hear a voice.

"I know you have been exploring my garden."

"You have seen the flowers."

"You have followed the pathways."

"You have discovered some of my memories."

"But I wonder what you think you have learned."

A pause.

"My experiences are complicated.

Some days are difficult.

Some days are overwhelming.

But I am more than either of those experiences."

The voice becomes softer.

"I am still here."

(if: $voiceHeard is false)[
    (set: $voiceHeard to true)
    (set: $awareness to $awareness + 1)
]

[[Continue->Final Question]]


:: Golden Clock [excess] {"position":"1000,975","size":"100,100"}
# THE GOLDEN CLOCK

A golden clock floats in the air.

Its hands spin rapidly.

You cannot tell whether time is moving forward or backward.

You look away for a moment.

When you look back, the clock has changed again.

(if: $clockFound is false)[
    (set: $clockFound to true)
    (set: $memory to $memory + 1)
]

A message appears:

"Do you remember how long you have been here?"

[[Follow the floating books->Floating Library]]


:: Golden Flower [excess] {"position":"1125,725","size":"100,100"}
# THE GOLDEN FLOWER

A glowing golden flower catches your attention.

It seems almost impossible to look away.

You reach toward it.

(if: $flowerFound is false)[
    (set: $flowerFound to true)
    (set: $ideas to $ideas + 1)
]

The flower glows brighter.

For a moment, everything feels possible.

You notice a staircase in the distance.

[[Continue toward the staircase->Infinite Staircase]]


:: Infinite Staircase [excess] {"position":"1000,850","size":"100,100"}
# THE INFINITE STAIRCASE

The staircase stretches upward beyond the clouds.

You begin climbing.

The higher you go, the more possibilities appear.

A castle.

A floating library.

An entire world waiting to be explored.

You feel as though you could accomplish everything.

But which direction should you take?

(set: $ideas to $ideas + 1)

[[Climb toward the golden clock->Golden Clock]]


